    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n2 4 2 4\n8\n2 4 3 4 2 5 3 1",
        "output": "8\n216",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There are 888 possible ordered quadruples. Two of them are:\n\n[i,j,k,l]=[2,3,4,1][i, j, k, l] = [2, 3, 4, 1][i,j,k,l]=[2,3,4,1]. For this AB =4⊕2=6= 4 \\oplus 2 = 6=4⊕2=6, BC =2⊕4=6= 2 \\oplus 4 = 6=2⊕4=6, CD =4⊕2=6= 4 \\oplus 2 = 6=4⊕2=6 and DA =2⊕4=6= 2 \\oplus 4 = 6=2⊕4=6. Since AB = CD and AC = BD, this is a rectangle.\n[i,j,k,l]=[2,1,4,3][i, j, k, l] = [2, 1, 4, 3][i,j,k,l]=[2,1,4,3]. For this AB =4⊕2=6= 4 \\oplus 2 = 6=4⊕2=6, BC =2⊕4=6= 2 \\oplus 4 = 6=2⊕4=6, CD =4⊕2=6= 4 \\oplus 2 = 6=4⊕2=6 and DA =2⊕4=6= 2 \\oplus 4 = 6=2⊕4=6. Since AB = CD and AC = BD, this is a rectangle.\n\nTest case 222: There are 216216216 possible ordered quadruples. One of them is:\n\n[i,j,k,l]=[4,6,5,7][i, j, k, l] = [4, 6, 5, 7][i,j,k,l]=[4,6,5,7]. For this AB =4⊕5=1= 4 \\oplus 5 = 1=4⊕5=1, BC =5⊕2=7= 5 \\oplus 2 = 7=5⊕2=7, CD =2⊕3=1= 2 \\oplus 3 = 1=2⊕3=1 and DA =3⊕4=7= 3 \\oplus 4 = 7=3⊕4=7. Since AB = CD and AC = BD, this is a rectangle."
      }
    ]
  },
